        "base": "https://www.wananga.com/feed/atom",
        "language": null,
        "type": "text/plain",
        "value": "<div data-rss-type=\"text\">\r\n  <h3>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Junior / Intermediate Application Systems Analyst \u2013\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </h3>\r\n  <h3>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            H\u0101pai Kaupapa -\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </span>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           CLOSED\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </h3>\r\n  <h4>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           \u014ctaki Campus\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </h4>\r\n</div>\r\n<div data-rss-type=\"text\">\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Te W\u0101nanga o Raukawa is seeking a motivated\u00a0\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           Junior / Intermediate Application Systems Analyst\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           \u00a0to join\u00a0\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           H\u0101pai Kaupapa\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           \u00a0in \u014ctaki.\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <br/>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           This role supports strategic projects across the W\u0101nanga by designing, building and improving digital solutions using\u00a0\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           Microsoft Power Platform, SharePoint Online and Microsoft 365\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           . You will work with project teams to develop apps, automations and dashboards that improve workflows and help kaimahi confidently engage with digital tools.\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <br/>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           M\u0101u e mau mai:\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <br/>\r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           A qualification in Information Systems, Computer Science, or a related field (or equivalent experience)\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Experience with\u00a0\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           Microsoft Power Platform (Power Apps, Power Automate, Power BI)\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Familiarity with\u00a0\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           SharePoint Online and Microsoft 365 tools\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Interest in system integration (experience with\u00a0\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           \u00a0is a bonus)\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to test, troubleshoot and support digital solutions\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Clear communication skills and the ability to support non-technical users\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <br/>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           E rapu ana m\u0101tou i t\u0113tahi tangata e:\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <br/>\r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Is curious, adaptable and eager to learn new technologies\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Enjoys building practical digital solutions and improving systems\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Works well independently and as part of a collaborative team\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Is committed to working within a kaupapa M\u0101ori environment\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <br/>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           Ka tukuna e m\u0101tou:\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <br/>\r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           A supportive, kaupapa-driven working environment\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Opportunities to grow your skills across\u00a0\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           Power Platform, Microsoft 365 and emerging AI tools\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           The chance to contribute to digital innovation that supports our W\u0101nanga community\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <br/>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Join us and help build the digital tools that support our tauira, kaimahi and kaupapa.\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <br/>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           Applications close:\u00a0Monday 30 March 2026\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <br/>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           For further information or to apply for this role, please contact:\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           \u00a0\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Sam Hata, Te Whare Tiaki Rawa\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           \u012am\u0113ra: sam.hata@twor.ac.nz\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Waea: 06 3649011\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <br/>\r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>"
      }
